{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.047,
            0.419,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.128
          ],
          "content": "In the rest of this chapter, we will assume that all the lengths are of a fixed unit unless specified otherwise."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.137,
            0.397,
            0.161
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ What is the value of $\\sqrt { 2 } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.173,
            0.514,
            0.199
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Decimal Representation of $\\sqrt { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.208,
            0.847,
            0.249
          ],
          "content": "The decimal representation of $\\sqrt { 2 }$ can be found using the following argument."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.258,
            0.48,
            0.281
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Is $\\sqrt { 2 }$ less than or greater than 1?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.283,
            0.849,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "A square of sidelength 1 unit has an area of 1 sq. unit. A square of sidelength In other w $\\sqrt { 2 }$ hs, $1 ^ { 2 } = 1$ area , and $\\sqrt { 2 } ^ { 2 } = \\bar { 2 }$ units. So, 1 is less than. $\\sqrt { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.409,
            0.345,
            0.589,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm { T h e r e f o r e } , 1 < { \\sqrt { 2 } } .",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.377,
            0.48,
            0.401
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Is $\\sqrt { 2 }$ less than or greater than 2?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.403,
            0.848,
            0.462
          ],
          "content": "A square of sidelength 2 units has an area of 4 sq. units. A square of sidelength $\\sqrt { 2 }$ has an area of 2 sq. units. So, 2 is greater than $\\sqrt { 2 }$ In other words, ${ \\sqrt { 2 } } ^ { 2 } = 2 ,$ , and $2 ^ { 2 } = 4 .$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.409,
            0.464,
            0.589,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{Therefore}, \\sqrt{2} < 2.",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.419,
            0.49,
            0.579,
            0.512
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{Thus}, 1 < \\sqrt{2} < 2.",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.516,
            0.677,
            0.538
          ],
          "content": "We call 1 a lower bound on $\\sqrt { 2 }$ and 2 an upper bound."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.547,
            0.493,
            0.57
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Can we find closer bounds for $\\sqrt { 2 } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.589,
            0.259,
            0.609
          ],
          "content": "1 . 1 ^ { 2 } = 1 . 2 1",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.39,
            0.59,
            0.508,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": "1.41^{2} = 4.9881",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.631,
            0.59,
            0.778,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": "1.411^{2} = 1.990921",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.613,
            0.262,
            0.632
          ],
          "content": "1 . 2 ^ { 2 } = 1 . 4 4",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.389,
            0.614,
            0.514,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": "1 . 4 2 ^ { 2 } = 2 . 0 1 \\dot { 6 } 4",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.631,
            0.614,
            0.778,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": "1.412^{2} = 1.993744",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_19.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.636,
            0.263,
            0.655
          ],
          "content": "1 . 3 ^ { 2 } = 1 . 6 9",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.389,
            0.64,
            0.569,
            0.663
          ],
          "content": "S \\bar { \\bigcirc } , 1 . 4 \\bar { 1 } < \\sqrt { 2 } < 1 . 4 2",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.631,
            0.638,
            0.782,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": "1.413^{2} = 1.996569",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_22.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.659,
            0.263,
            0.679
          ],
          "content": "1.4^{2} = 1.96",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_23.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.631,
            0.661,
            0.782,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": "1.414^{2} = 1.999396",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_24.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.683,
            0.266,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": "1 . 5 ^ { 2 } = 2 . 2 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_25.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.631,
            0.684,
            0.789,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": "1 . 4 1 5 ^ { 2 } = 2 . 0 0 2 2 2 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_26.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.709,
            0.337,
            0.73
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{SO},   1.4 < \\sqrt{2} < 1.5",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_27.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.63,
            0.711,
            0.818,
            0.732
          ],
          "content": "\\mathsf { S o } ,   1 . 4 1 4 < \\sqrt { 2 } < 1 . 4 1 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_28.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.749,
            0.846,
            0.789
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Will we ever get a number with a terminating decimal representation whose square is 2?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.792,
            0.848,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": "If there is such a terminating decimal starting with 1.414… whose square is 2, then it must have a non-zero last digit. If this is the case, then the decimal representation of its square will also have a non-zero last digit after the decimal point. For example, if $\\sqrt { 2 }$ is of the form 1.414…4, then its square will be of the form —"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.34,
            0.886,
            0.654,
            0.918
          ],
          "content": "\\bigsqcup \\cdot \\bigsqcup \\quad \\bigsqcup \\quad \\cdots \\quad \\bigsqcup \\quad 6",
          "image_source": "images/page_5_equation_31.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.094,
            0.921,
            0.129,
            0.942
          ],
          "content": "38"
        }
      ]
    }
